Where a file could be read as falling under both, the code license governs the
executable content and the data license governs the benchmark rollouts, grades,
and prose.

Rationale: code carries an OSI-approved license because reproducibility norms
(and anyone who wants to run this environment) expect one, while the graded
rollout corpus remains noncommercial.

Model outputs contained in the dataset remain subject to the terms of the
provider that produced them.
